### Trade-Offs in the Restoration Process

1. **Noise Reduction vs. Detail Preservation**:
   - **Noise Reduction**: Aggressive noise reduction techniques can smooth out noise but may also blur important image details, leading to a loss of sharpness and clarity.
   - **Detail Preservation**: Techniques that focus on preserving image details may leave some noise in the image, which can be visually distracting.

2. **Parameter Tuning**:
   - **Wiener Filter Parameter `K`**: The parameter `K` in the Wiener filter controls the balance between noise reduction and detail preservation. A smaller `K` value means more aggressive restoration, which can amplify noise. A larger `K` value means more conservative restoration, which may not fully recover the original image details.
   - **CLS Regularization Parameter `lambda`**: The regularization parameter `lambda` in CLS filtering helps stabilize the restoration process. A higher `lambda` can overly smooth the image, while a lower `lambda` may not sufficiently reduce noise.
   - **TV Denoising Parameters**: The `Amount` and `Radius` parameters in TV denoising control the degree of sharpening and the radius of the effect. Overuse can lead to over-smoothing and loss of fine details.

### Improved MATLAB Code

To make the code more modular and avoid hardcoded values, we will define functions for each step of the restoration process. This will improve readability and reusability.

```matlab
% Function to read and preprocess the image
function [im, degraded] = preprocess_image(filename, nn)
    % Read the original image
    im = imread(filename);
    im = im2double(im); % Convert to double precision for processing

    % Apply the degradation process
    x = fft2(im);
    x(10, 10) = x(10, 10) + nn;
    x(10, 11) = x(10, 11) + nn;
    x(11, 10) = x(11, 10) + nn;
    x(11, 11) = x(11, 11) + nn;
    degraded = real(ifft2(x));
end

% Function to define the degradation function H
function H = define_degradation_function(nn, im)
    H = ones(size(im)); % Initialize the degradation function
    H(10, 10) = H(10, 10) + nn / abs(fft2(im)(10, 10));
    H(10, 11) = H(10, 11) + nn / abs(fft2(im)(10, 11));
    H(11, 10) = H(11, 10) + nn / abs(fft2(im)(11, 10));
    H(11, 11) = H(11, 11) + nn / abs(fft2(im)(11, 11));
end

% Function to apply Wiener filtering
function restored = wiener_filter(degraded, H, K)
    Y = fft2(degraded);
    G = conj(H) ./ (abs(H).^2 + K);
    restored = real(ifft2(G .* Y));
end

% Function to apply Constrained Least Squares (CLS) filtering
function restored = cls_filter(degraded, H, lambda)
    H_fft = fft2(H, size(degraded, 1), size(degraded, 2));
    Y = fft2(degraded);
    restored = real(ifft2((conj(H_fft) .* Y) ./ (abs(H_fft).^2 + lambda)));
end

% Function to apply Total Variation (TV) denoising
function restored = tv_denoising(image, amount, radius)
    restored = imsharpen(image, 'Amount', amount, 'Radius', radius);
end

% Function to calculate MSE and SSIM
function [mse, ssim] = calculate_metrics(original, restored)
    mse = mean((original - restored).^2);
    ssim = ssim(original, restored);
end

% Main script
filename = 'saturn.tif';
nn = 1 * 1e+6;

% Preprocess the image
[im, degraded] = preprocess_image(filename, nn);

% Display the degraded image
figure;
imshow(degraded, []);
title('Degraded Image');

% Define the degradation function H
H = define_degradation_function(nn, im);

% Wiener filtering for restoration
K = 0.01; % Noise-to-signal power ratio (adjust as needed)
restored_wiener = wiener_filter(degraded, H, K);

% Display the restored image using Wiener filtering
figure;
imshow(restored_wiener, []);
title('Restored Image (Wiener Filter)');

% Constrained Least Squares (CLS) filtering for restoration
lambda = 0.01; % Regularization parameter (adjust as needed)
restored_cls = cls_filter(degraded, H, lambda);

% Display the restored image using CLS filtering
figure;
imshow(restored_cls, []);
title('Restored Image (CLS Filter)');

% Total Variation (TV) denoising for restoration
amount = 0.5; % Amount of sharpening (adjust as needed)
radius = 1;   % Radius of the effect (adjust as needed)
restored_tv = tv_denoising(restored_cls, amount, radius);

% Display the restored image using TV denoising
figure;
imshow(restored_tv, []);
title('Restored Image (TV Denoising)');

% Display the original image for comparison
figure;
imshow(im, []);
title('Original Image');

% Calculate MSE and SSIM for visual assessment
[mse_wiener, ssim_wiener] = calculate_metrics(im, restored_wiener);
[mse_cls, ssim_cls] = calculate_metrics(im, restored_cls);
[mse_tv, ssim_tv] = calculate_metrics(im, restored_tv);

disp(['Mean Squared Error (MSE) - Wiener: ', num2str(mse_wiener)]);
disp(['Structural Similarity Index (SSIM) - Wiener: ', num2str(ssim_wiener)]);

disp(['Mean Squared Error (MSE) - CLS: ', num2str(mse_cls)]);
disp(['Structural Similarity Index (SSIM) - CLS: ', num2str(ssim_cls)]);

disp(['Mean Squared Error (MSE) - TV: ', num2str(mse_tv)]);
disp(['Structural Similarity Index (SSIM) - TV: ', num2str(ssim_tv)]);

% Iterative Refinement
for i = 1:5 % Number of iterations
    % Wiener filtering
    restored_wiener = wiener_filter(restored_tv, H, K);

    % CLS filtering
    restored_cls = cls_filter(restored_wiener, H, lambda);

    % TV denoising
    restored_tv = tv_denoising(restored_cls, amount, radius);

    % Display the restored image after each iteration
    figure;
    imshow(restored_tv, []);
    title(['Restored Image (Iteration ', num2str(i), ')']);

    % Calculate MSE and SSIM for each iteration
    [mse_tv_iter, ssim_tv_iter] = calculate_metrics(im, restored_tv);

    disp(['Mean Squared Error (MSE) - Iteration ', num2str(i), ': ', num2str(mse_tv_iter)]);
    disp(['Structural Similarity Index (SSIM) - Iteration ', num2str(i), ': ', num2str(ssim_tv_iter)]);
end
```

### Explanation

1. **Modular Functions**:
   - **`preprocess_image`**: Reads and preprocesses the image, applying the degradation process.
   - **`define_degradation_function`**: Defines the degradation function `H` based on the original image.
   - **`wiener_filter`**: Applies Wiener filtering to the degraded image.
   - **`cls_filter`**: Applies Constrained Least Squares (CLS) filtering to the degraded image.
   - **`tv_denoising`**: Applies Total Variation (TV) denoising to the image.
